{"_id":"68a7360a8ec3d8323af11700","nodeId":"M1CU2Yq6dLp4yOuGV0fhF","roadmapSlug":"angular","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:50.309Z","description":"# Reusable Animations\n\nTo create a reusable animation, use the `animation()` function to define an animation in a separate .ts file and declare this animation definition as a const export variable. You can then import and reuse this animation in any of your application components using the `useAnimation()` function.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Reusable Animations","url":"https://angular.dev/guide/animations/reusable-animations","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0da4"},{"type":"article","title":"Reusable Animations with Angular","url":"https://catalincodes.com/posts/reusable-animations-with-angular","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0da5"},{"type":"video","title":"Angular Animations: Creating reusable animations!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ObYCutiBOTo","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0da6"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:01:05.151Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/angular/content/M1CU2Yq6dLp4yOuGV0fhF.md"}